# PDP Versions (v1 frozen … v4 active)

The PDP ships four comparison routes on one deploy:

- **v1** (`/v1`, legacy `/`) — frozen brand baseline
- **v2** (`/v2`) — first stakeholder pivot (frozen)
- **v3** (`/v3`) — Paper r4 pivot (frozen)
- **v4** (`/v4`) — Paper r5 / latest feedback round — **active work**

**Docs (read before edits):**

- Architecture & flags: `docs/pdp-versions.md`
- Deploy & links: `docs/deploy-and-links.md`
- Playbook: `docs/prototype-versions.md`
- Round changelogs: `docs/rounds/`

## Rules

- Read `docs/pdp-versions.md` before editing any PDP code.
- New round work goes in `src/components/pdp/version/` or behind flags in `pdp-version-config.ts`. Never rewrite v1/v2/v3 defaults.
- Do not branch on `version === "v2"` / `"v3"` / `"v4"` across the codebase. Add a flag to `PdpVersionConfig`.
- Never edit `pdp-data.ts` or `pdp-section-chapters.ts` for new-round needs.
- Never add version-only CSS to `globals.css`. Use `src/app/vN/pdp-vN.css` scoped under `[data-pdp-version="vN"]`. Treat `globals.css` edits as cross-version.
- Shared `pdp-v2-*` components render on `/v2`, `/v3`, and `/v4` — gate v4-only layout behind v4 flags.
- After any change, confirm older routes still match baseline, then run `pnpm check:versions`.
- Before stakeholder share: follow pre-ship checklist in `docs/deploy-and-links.md` (`vercel --prod` updates production).

## Quick map

- Provider/hook: `src/components/pdp/version/pdp-version-context.tsx` (`usePdpVersion()`)
- Config adapter: `src/components/pdp/version/pdp-version-config.ts` (`getPdpVersionConfig(version)`)
- v2 slides: `src/components/pdp/version/pdp-data-v2.ts`
- v2 chapters: `src/components/pdp/version/pdp-section-chapters-v2.ts`
- v3 hero/CTA/color-sheet: `src/components/pdp/version/pdp-v3-*.tsx`
- v4 specs: `src/components/pdp/version/pdp-v4-specs.ts`
- Boundary checks: `scripts/check-pdp-version-boundaries.mjs`
